1	//! Deterministic pack emission: merged records → the portable artifact.
2	//!
3	//! A pack is a directory (a zip of it later) that ANY tool can consume:
4	//! sharded `records-*.jsonl`, a `manifest.json` with per-file sha256s, the
5	//! recipe that built it, the suggestion files (`mapping.suggested.json`,
6	//! `relations.jsonl`, `suggestions.md`), and a `SHA256SUMS` over
7	//! everything. Determinism is
8	//! the load-bearing property: shard assignment is `xxh3_64(id) % shards`,
9	//! records are id-ordered, and every record carries the SAME key set (a
10	//! key absent from one record is `[]` for array keys, `null` otherwise) —
11	//! so an unchanged input rebuilds byte-identical shard files, and the
12	//! `_id`s the engine derives stay stable across rebuilds (autoindex
13	//! clusters datasets by field-name set; an omitted optional field would
14	//! silently move a record between datasets).
15	//!
16	//! `manifest.json` and `SHA256SUMS` necessarily vary (timestamp,
17	//! generation) — determinism is claimed for the RECORDS, never the wrapper.
18	//!
19	//! Reading a pack back ([`read_manifest`]) is the consumption half of
20	//! `xerj corpus add --from <pack>`: checksum-verify EVERYTHING the manifest
21	//! and SHA256SUMS claim, refusing loudly on any mismatch, because a pack is
22	//! an artifact that traveled — disk, download, or release attachment —
23	//! before it got here.
24	
