1	//! `xerj corpus build` — build a portable corpus pack from harvested records.
2	//!
3	//! The pipeline, end to end:
4	//!
5	//! ```text
6	//! recipe.toml ─→ harvest (dir walk / M2: http-zip, git)
7	//!             ─→ normalize (format adapter: osv | flat)
8	//!             ─→ store     (content-addressed, presence = dedup)
9	//!             ─→ identity  (union-find over declared edge values)
10	//!             ─→ merge     (precedence + array union + strictest licence)
11	//!             ─→ suggest   (mapping + join-key hints from a sample — never applied)
12	//!             ─→ pack      (deterministic sharded JSONL + manifest + SUMS)
13	//!
14	//! Publishing is a separate step, never part of a build:
15	//! `xerj corpus sign <pack-dir> --key <seed-file>` writes the detached
16	//! ed25519 signature over SHA256SUMS (see `sign.rs`); `xerj corpus add
17	//! --from <pack> --verify-sig <pubkey-file>` checks it on the way in.
18	//! ```
19	//!
20	//! Incrementality is not a mode, it is the storage layout: every normalized
21	//! record lands at `store/<slug>.<xxh3-of-canonical-json>.json`, so a re-run
22	//! recomputes the key, sees the file, and skips. Deleting the source tree's
23	//! unchanged files and re-running is a no-op beyond the walk; the pack is
24	//! then rebuilt from the store deterministically.
25	//!
26	//! The tool is domain-agnostic by directive: what a "record" is, which
27	//! fields are identity, and how fields merge all live in the recipe, never
28	//! here. Licence terms ride along as record data (`licence`, per-source
29	//! `sources[]`); the tool does not and must not enforce them — the pack
30	//! author owns what goes in the pack.
31	
32	pub mod httpget;
33	pub mod identity;
34	pub mod normalize;
35	pub mod pack;
36	pub mod recipe;
37	pub mod sign;
38	pub mod source;
39	pub mod store;
40	pub mod suggest;
